## 1. Book text (third-party copyrighted works)

`references/book-knowledge.sqlite` contains the full extracted text of two
commercial books, reproduced there only for personal research assistance:

1. Barbara Gastel and Robert A. Day, *How to Write and Publish a Scientific
   Paper*, 8th edition (Cambridge University Press, 2016),
   ISBN 978-1-316-64043-2, DOI 10.1017/9781108105293
   (`urn:isbn:9781316640432`).
2. Kate L. Turabian, *A Manual for Writers of Research Papers, Theses, and
   Dissertations: Chicago Style for Students and Researchers*, 7th edition
   (University of Chicago Press, 2003; 2007 paperback printing),
   ISBN 978-0-226-82337-9 (`urn:isbn:9780226823379`).

All rights in those books remain with their respective copyright holders.
Nothing in this repository transfers any right in them. Use of the extracted
text is limited to:

- private, non-commercial study, writing assistance, and research;
- querying, paraphrasing, and citation of the books' *advice* as an aid to
  your own writing;
- rebuilding the index on your own machine from legally obtained copies of
  the books.

You may not publish, redistribute, sublicense, sell, or otherwise make
available the book text, the SQLite database, or derivative extracts of it,
in whole or in part, to any third party, in any medium.

